    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d847">

                <pb facs="0866" n="608" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg608"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 341.115Am319</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Great
                        Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-11-02T16:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 2, 1915, 4 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2390. Department informed steamer <hi rendition="#italic">Hocking</hi> registered
                    under American flag was seized by British cruiser while <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >en route</hi> in ballast to Norfolk to load coal under charter to Argentine
                    Republic, and taken to Halifax. You will request of British Government
                    explanation at once of seizure of this vessel.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
